<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Philippi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">42 BCE</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberators-civil-war">Liberators' civil war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Philippi was fought in October 42 BCE near the city of Philippi in eastern Macedonia. The forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Octavian defeated the army of Brutus and Cassius, assassins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, in two engagements, after which both killed themselves. The victory ended the republican cause and left the triumvirs masters of the Roman world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi.jpg" alt="Battle of Philippi" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Marsyas assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philippi_location.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
